# Ibex bring-up (hw/soc, docs/38). Same rule as tt/tt/ above: fetched in
# for a check, not vendored. `ext/` is TWO upstream git clones -- Ibex,
# and riscv-formal since docs/63 -- `tools/` is two downloaded
# toolchains (sv2v, riscv-none-elf-gcc), and `gen/`, `out/` are
# regenerated by hw/soc/flow/. The tracked sources are
# hw/soc/{flow,rtl,tb,syn,sta,fi,rvformal}/ and hw/soc/tools.soc.mk,
# which pins every one of the fetched things by commit or sha256 so that
# what is ignored is still reproducible.
hw/soc/ext/
hw/soc/tools/
hw/soc/gen/
# hw/soc/genrvfi/ is the SAME sv2v conversion of the SAME pinned Ibex
# commit with --define=RVFI added, so the core carries the 45 RVFI trace
# ports riscv-formal binds to (docs/63). It is a SECOND tree and not a
# replacement: hw/soc/gen/ must go on reproducing byte-identically,
# because every area, timing and campaign number from docs/38 to
# docs/62 was measured from it.
hw/soc/genrvfi/
# hw/soc/genp/ is gen/ibex_top.v with the register file's fault port
# added, written by flow/ibex_fault_port.py (docs/44 section 4). Same
# rule: derived from a pinned input by a tracked script, never
# vendored and never edited by hand.
hw/soc/genp/
# hw/soc/gen_spi_host/ is the sv2v conversion of OpenTitan's spi_host
# closure at the commit hw/soc/tools.soc.mk pins, written by
# hw/soc/flow/sv2v_spi_host.sh (docs/65). Same rule as gen/: derived
# from a pinned input by a tracked script, never vendored.
hw/soc/gen_spi_host/
hw/soc/out/

